cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use TimeGym, cite the software and record the version and source commit
  or the source fingerprint in your report. The manuscript in paper/ is a working
  paper; this metadata does not assert that it has been published or has a DOI.
version: 1.2.0
date-released: 2026-11-10
type: software
title: "TimeGym: verification and diagnosis for forecasting pipelines"
authors:
  - family-names: Seca
    given-names: Diogo
repository-code: "https://github.com/diogoseca/timegym"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - time series
  - forecasting
  - verification
  - probabilistic forecasting
  - scientific software
abstract: >-
  TimeGym checks forecasting output contracts, conditional references, and
  declared metamorphic properties. It supports point forecasts, marginal
  quantiles, coherent joint samples, retained visual experiments, and JSON
  diagnostic reports with replay information.
references:
  - type: article
    title: "TimeGym: Debugging for Time Series Modeling in Python"
    authors:
      - family-names: Seca
        given-names: Diogo
    year: 2021
    doi: "10.48550/arXiv.2105.01404"
    url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2105.01404v1"
